!Modula2 -- Modula-2 on the BOX

Modula-2 (PIM 4 and ISO 10514-1) compiled to machine code in memory by
LLVM and run at once, inside the box.  The compiler is MacModula2's.

Files
  &A7B Modula2   a program module or an implementation module (.mod)
  &A7C M2Def     a definition module (.def)
  Double-click a program to run it: its output appears in a TaskWindow;
  a program that makes a Declaritive window runs as a task of its own.
  The modules a program imports are found beside it (Name/def and
  Name/mod, or def.Name and mod.Name), then in the standard library.

The command
  *Modula2 [-c] [-t] [-O0..3] <file> [<arguments>]
    -c       compile only and report errors as  file:line: error: text
    -t       give the compile time
    -O0..-O3 LLVM's optimisation (default -O2)
  Escape stops a program (as HALT).  A fault ends the run, not the box.

The library
  The ISO library (STextIO, SWholeIO, SRealIO, TextIO, SeqFile,
  StreamFile, RndFile, Strings, EXCEPTIONS, COROUTINES, ...), PIM's
  (InOut, ...), and two of the box's own:
  SWI          RISC OS SWIs by name or number, registers in and out:
               Call raises an exception on an error, XCall returns the
               error block.  Str copies a string for a SWI, GetStr reads
               one back, Addr checks that an address is RISC OS's.
               NEW'd memory and global variables are in a dynamic area
               ("Modula-2") and can be given to SWIs.
  Declaritive  desktop windows described in JSON (the Declaritive
               module): Init, Add, Create, Set, Get, Poll, CloseDown.
  Their definition modules are in the ROM, /usr/lib/modula2/boxdef.

Not on the box
  Cocoa, Objective-C, COM and Win32, inline x86 assembler, and building
  executables (programs are always compiled and run).

Examples
  Hello, SWIs, Files, Classes, Coroutines, Exceptions, Bench, Greeter.
